                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "237974540",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198104522380",
                            "num_reviews": 46,
                            "playtime_forever": 860,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 860,
                            "last_played": 1792278795
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Ahh the continuation of the Blackwell story, or should I say backstory because this takes place before the first game. This felt like a more mature game than the first, both in the sence that it builds uponand improves on the first games story and mechanics but also that the story feels more mature, like the persons in it actually are real people with real life problems and hardships. I felt the 70's setting and the lack of computers and internet as a source of information to aid in the investigative process made the phonebook and telephone investigation interface more time period relevant, but it also made ME the player feel like I deducted something crucial when I put in the right input there to take the investigation forward. Also I felt that Lauren in spite of her flaws and vises was a much more interesting main character than Rosangela from the first game as she had fully embraced the role as a medium and all that entails for her worldview. This game also served a purpose to answer a few of the loose end questions you had after playing Blackwell Legacy. But it of course didn't answer all the questions you had and it also introduced a few unanswered questions of its own when you had finished the game.\r\nThis made me look forward to playing the next Blackwell game.",
